course: dictionary
lesson: 14413
title: Overgrown
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Overgrown describes a place that has grown too much, usually because no one has cut it back. «The garden gate was hidden under weeds, because nobody had cut the grass for years.» The garden is overgrown: plants have grown over everything.
explain: The clues are in the sentence. Hidden, weeds and nobody had cut all tell you the plants grew wild. Ask yourself what would fit here, then swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Overgrown can also describe a person. «He is a grown man, but he sulks like an overgrown schoolboy.» Here it means grown up in size but still acting like a child.
fact: Overgrown means covered with plants, weeds or grass that have grown too much because no one has cut them.
fact: Overgrown can also mean grown too large.
fact: «An overgrown schoolboy» means someone who is grown up but acts like a child.
fact: In stories, an overgrown garden or castle often tells the reader that a place is old, forgotten or secret.
fact: Overgrown places can hide holes, nettles, ticks or snakes, so be careful when you go into one.
exercise: «The path was overgrown, so we could not see where it led.» What does overgrown mean here? | Made of stone | Very wide and smooth | *Covered with weeds and plants that nobody had cut | Painted in bright colours
exercise: «He is grown up, but he sulks like an overgrown schoolboy.» What does overgrown suggest? | Happy and kind | Very small and quiet | *Grown up in size, but acting like a child | Old and cracked
exercise: «The old castle was hidden in overgrown ivy and thick weeds.» Why was the castle hard to find? | It was brand new | It was built on a hill of sand | It was painted bright green | *Plants had grown over it because nobody had cut them back
test: «Our tree house was overgrown, so we had to push through the branches to get in.» What does overgrown mean? | *Covered with plants that nobody had cut | Painted in bright colours | Brand new and shiny | Made of wood
test: Which is a good reason to be careful in an overgrown field? | The grass is too short to hide anything | It is too new to have any plants | It is too bright to see | *Snakes, ticks and holes could be hidden in it
exam: Lila says overgrown means brand new. What is the best answer? | It means very quiet | It means very hungry | *It means plants have grown too much because no one has cut them | It means brand new and shiny
